      "message": "Good work! This has been a long-standing correctness issue that is nice to have resolved.\n\nAs some follow-up work with this split, we have more flexibility in what uniforms we use to represent the transforms:\n\n - For the non-persp case, we can do 3 vec2\u0027s (2 rows of the upper 2x2 and translation), so the math simplifies to `{dot(row1, x1), dot(row2, xy)} + t`\n - For the persp case, we are always doing z\u003d0, so we could flatten the 4x4 to a 3x3 at this point and not lose any information.",
